 :dispositions
 [{:id :prior-gap :status :confirmed :detail "Prior bounded discovery is materially supported: inspected sources supply neither an authenticated owner-bound issuer nor real revocation/commit/release fence. This does not claim global absence."}
  {:id :separation :status :retain :detail "Axxium identity, Emacs resource consent and native owner order, and GovOne governance are separate; Sol is a possible fixed carrier, not a consent issuer. No label, callback, identity claim or preflight is authority."}
  {:id :durability :status :retain-held :detail "No real persistent adapter, anti-rollback or single-writer fencing has been demonstrated. A durable consume-before-mutation can provide at-most-one admitted attempt under proven storage assumptions, not exactly-once effects; partial writes and lost responses remain indeterminate."}
  {:id :runtime :status :held :detail "Keep public dispatch denied and dormant Emacs code unloaded; no raw eval, generic command, shell, unrestricted IPC, replacement identity/policy/ledger kernel, existing user buffer or i3 effect. Synthetic tests cannot qualify native custody or real owner ordering."}]
 :findings
 [{:id :f1-exact-boundary-shapes :severity :blocking-design :plan-lines [26 29 30 31 33 35]
   :defect "The plan lists fields and verbs but does not define the closed, typed owner-facing invocation, operator approval, grant state, revoke result and release decision shapes or their canonical binding and state transitions. In particular Axxium's actual returned context has no generation; GovOne's actual Decision has a bundle version, not an editor-specific signed, request-bound release lease. Labels for a future bridge or callback cannot fill those gaps. This is an incomplete design, not an assertion that the plan claims these already exist."
   :minimal-fix "Before implementation admission, specify a closed versioned typed contract and trust provenance per field, fixed read versus replace operation variants, exact canonical bytes/encoding and binding, object/epoch/revision ownership, grant states and allowed transitions, authenticated operator issuance and revoke ACK, selected credential/session identity and generation derivation, and governed destination/decision custody and validity. Map each field and transition to actual owner APIs or explicitly mark it missing and deny; no client-supplied field or adapter assertion substitutes for owner authority. Define the native compare-and-effect/release linearization, including the precise first trusted custody boundary."
   :red-oracle "Synthetic two actors, two credentials for one actor, and two operator grants: swap one binding or forged generation at a time, alter canonical request or output destination, inject duplicate/unknown fields, or replay a consumed/revoked grant; assert zero native mutation and zero released bytes, and include a separately admitted exact positive control. Doubles test the protocol only."}
  {:id :f2-clock-and-expiry :severity :blocking-design :plan-lines [27 29 33 34 36 50]
   :defect "Issue/expiry and clock faults are named, but the trusted clock, expiry comparison point, rollback/uncertainty behavior and relationship to identity or governance validity during a delayed finite fence are not specified. A grant checked while fresh can expire after a blocking durable consume but before mutation or disclosure."
   :minimal-fix "Specify trusted time source and maximum uncertainty, owner-epoch clock continuity, fail-closed rollback/unavailable behavior, and check expiry at the native effect/first-release linearization after potentially blocking steps. Bound or invalidate any identity/governance admission whose lifetime cannot cover that point; owner restart invalidates old handles/grants as already required."
   :red-oracle "Use a deterministic fake clock: approve before expiry, pause after durable consume, advance through expiry, then resume; assert zero mutation or disclosure and consumed grant cannot replay. Repeat with clock regression, unavailable time, and a qualified synthetic governance lease expiring at release; include an unexpired exact positive control."}
  {:id :f3-stale-authorization-gate :severity :process :plan-lines [38 39 41 42 43 54 58]
   :defect "The plan makes routine exact-source and owner extensions contingent on asking for new permission, despite the current standing authorization for recommended required reviewed owner-source extensions and bounded qualification. This introduces an obsolete permission blocker; it does not waive real independent review, scope, consent, synthetic limits or the present source-only assignment."
   :minimal-fix "Replace routine permission requests with exact owner/path selection, independent review, preservation and explicit recorded qualification/effect admission under standing authorization. Ask only when genuinely missing intent, human authentication or irreducible policy choice remains. This review itself authorizes no implementation, native load, effects or widening of its assignment."
   :red-oracle "Synthetic planning table: a necessary reviewed source-only owner extension with known exact paths and standing authorization proceeds without a routine user prompt; unknown owner/path, absent required review, missing human authentication, spending or a requested personal capture remains blocked for the appropriate reason. No product or runtime action is exercised."}]
 :admission-limits {:design "Revise the three findings and obtain independent exact-source design review; the plan is a safe direction, not a qualified executable owner seam. Unresolved integrations remain explicit blockers, not defects asserted to be already solved."
                    :native "Real owner must demonstrate exclusive relevant actions and atomic final comparison with native effect or first actual trusted release. A JS preflight, private mutex, synthetic callback or a version string alone is insufficient."
                    :identity "All relevant Axxium invalidations must participate in a proven owner admission order before the promised capability-specific acknowledgement; current Axxium endpoint response is not that proof. Credential expiry, session deletion, actor disablement, disconnect and recovery require exact coverage or denial."
                    :persistence "Do not claim persisted revocation, anti-rollback, unique single-use or post-restart safety until actual custody, durable commit, fencing and recovery are verified. If unavailable, retain deny; do not create another ledger."
                    :governance "No read release until actual matching GovOne decision and policy-change/release ordering are qualified; routing permission is neither resource consent nor automatic authorization for arbitrary destination."
                    :effects "Further real-owner qualification follows standing authorization only within separately recorded exact bounded admissions and remaining gates; no live server, buffers, credentials, sockets, source loading or tests were touched in this review."}
